---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy — WellRoost"
	description="What WellRoost records when you use the decision engines, what it does not, and how to turn any of it off."
>
	<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 lg:px-8">
		<p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.28em] font-semibold text-blue-700">Privacy</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-1000 sm:text-4xl">
			What we record, and what we do not.
		</h1>
		<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-gray-600">
			Effective 20 October 2026. The short version: the calculators work without handing over anything, the
			numbers you type stay in your browser unless you ask us to email them, and there are no advertising
			networks or cross-site trackers on this site.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-1000">Analytics &amp; telemetry</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-gray-600">
			We record anonymous interaction events and model parameters to evaluate calculator accuracy and refine our
			decision engines. We do not sell personal data or run cross-site tracking scripts.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-gray-600">
			Concretely, when you use an interactive asset we may record: which asset was opened, when it was opened,
			<strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900">the names of the input fields you changed</strong> (for example
			“compAverageValue”) and how many, the page you arrived from, your approximate viewport width, and a
			timestamp. We do <strong class="font-semibold text-gray-900">not</strong> record the values you type, your
			name, your address, or anything that identifies you. These events use no cookies and are not shared with
			advertising networks.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-1000">Your calculator inputs</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-gray-600">
			Multivariable engines save your inputs in your own browser (<code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.8em]">localStorage</code>)
			so that a return visit resumes where you left off. That data never leaves your device unless you explicitly
			ask us to email a scenario. Choosing “Start fresh”, clearing site data, or using a private window removes it.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-1000">Email</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-gray-600">
			Email is optional and only requested after a model is complete — never as a gate. If you ask for a scenario
			report, we store your address with the scenario you submitted, use it to send that report, and nothing else.
			You can unsubscribe at any time, and asking us to delete the record removes it.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-1000">What we do not do</h2>
		<ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 text-sm leading-7 text-gray-600">
			<li>No account, login, or session profile.</li>
			<li>No advertising pixels, retargeting, or cross-site tracking scripts.</li>
			<li>No selling or renting of personal data — we have no data to sell beyond an address you chose to give.</li>
			<li>No recording of the financial values you enter into the engines.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-1000">Retention and requests</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-gray-600">
			Interaction events are kept for up to 24 months in aggregate form. Email records are kept until you
			unsubscribe or ask for deletion. To request a copy or deletion of anything associated with your address,
			write to <a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-gray-900" href="mailto:privacy@wellroost.com">privacy@wellroost.com</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-1000">Changes</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-gray-600">
			If what we collect changes, this page changes with it and the effective date above moves. The date is the
			version recorded alongside any email you submit, so a record always answers to the notice it was given under.
		</p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
